Section 1. That Section 2.08.010, Appointment and term
— Removal
— Vacancy, ofChapter
2.08, City Officers and Employees Generally, ofTitle 2, Administration and Personnel, ofthe code
of the city of Cheyenne, Wyoming, is amended as set out in this ordinance. Provisions currently
existing within Chapter 2.08 not set out within this ordinance remain unchanged.
2.08.0 10
Appointment and term
— Removal
— Vacancy.
A.
At the first regular meeting ofthe governing body in the official year following the
city election, or at such other times as needed to fill an appointed position set forth
in this section, there shall be appointed by the mayor, by and with the consent of
the city council, the following officers: city clerk, city treasurer, city engineer, city
attorney, fire chief, police chief, judge ofthe municipal court, judge ofthe juvenile
court, public works director, planning services director, parks and recrcation
director, development director, planning and development director, support
services director, community recreation and events director, and such other
officers and employees as are necessary for the efficient operation of the city.
Section 2.
That this ordinance shall be in full force and effect upon its passage and
publication.
